---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";

export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Full passive (all tenses, passive reporting) · B2 Grammar",
  "slug": "full-passive",
  "level": "B2",
  "topic": "Full passive (all tenses, passive reporting)",
  "category": "Grammar",
  "contentType": "grammar",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Control passive forms across aspect, tense, and modality and use impersonal or personal passive reporting structures to package information formally.",
  "sequence": 3,
  "prerequisites": ["b1/passive-voice", "b1/reported-speech", "b1/present-perfect-continuous"],
  "related": ["b2/reported-speech", "b2/register-and-formality"],
  "assessments": ["b2-exit"],
  "tutorReviewRequired": true,
  "qualityReview": {
    "status": "editorial-review",
    "generatedPedagogy": true,
    "learnerPilotCount": 0,
    "scoredItemCount": 75,
    "revisionSummary": "Passive aspect and modality, agency, heavy-chain recasting, passive types, reporting time, U.S. speech, listening, evidence, production, and retrieval were audited; three pilots remain."
  }
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 03</p>
  <h1>The <em>full passive</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A passive does not erase time, aspect, modality, or responsibility. It changes which participant becomes the grammatical topic. At B2, the challenge is to preserve the whole auxiliary system, choose active or passive focus deliberately, and report claims without making uncertainty sound like fact.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">70–80 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">tense · aspect · modality</span>
    <span class="tag">focus · agency · reporting</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min extension</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Track one event through several passive chains.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Preserve tense, aspect, and modality.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Decide</b><span>Foreground or restore the responsible agent.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Report</b><span>Package sourced claims with accurate time.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can build simple, progressive, perfect, future, and modal passives; recover every auxiliary; recast grammatical but overloaded chains; decide whether an agent is unknown, obvious, irrelevant, informative, or being concealed; distinguish event, result-state, and conversational <span class="ex">get</span>-passives; use two-object and prepositional passives; switch between impersonal and personal reporting; locate simultaneous, ongoing, earlier, and earlier-passive reported events; hear reduced U.S. forms; and deliver a sourced institutional briefing.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the affected participant, a useful agent, the irregular participle written, and the present-perfect-continuous auxiliary chain.">
    <h3>Reactivate the B1 passive foundation</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the grammatical role or complete verb family named in each prompt.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Passive foundation choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the affected participant">the affected participant</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="by engineer Lena Ortiz">by engineer Lena Ortiz</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="written">written</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has been reviewing">has been reviewing</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>In <span class="ex">The bridge was inspected</span>, the subject <span class="ex">the bridge</span> is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the affected participant" data-hint="The bridge receives the effect of the inspection rather than performing it." data-fix="The bridge is the affected participant and passive subject." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The agent adds professional authority in <span class="ex">The safety certificate was signed <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="by engineer Lena Ortiz" data-hint="A named qualified signer supplies useful source information." data-fix="The certificate was signed by engineer Lena Ortiz." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Complete the irregular family: <span class="ex">write, wrote, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="written" data-hint="The passive requires the past participle, the third form of write." data-fix="The family is write, wrote, written." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button></span>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The active present perfect continuous chain in <span class="ex">The committee <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has been reviewing" data-hint="Use has, been, and the -ing activity for an active process continuing to now." data-fix="The committee has been reviewing the plan." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the plan</span> will help you compare longer passive chains.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice what stays and what changes</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>One fictional station project at four stages</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">The crew is replacing the east elevator.</span><br /><span class="ex">The east elevator is being replaced.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">The crew has installed 18 platform lights.</span><br /><span class="ex">Eighteen platform lights have been installed.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">The contractor should have tested the emergency signs.</span><br /><span class="ex">The emergency signs should have been tested.</span></p>
    <p><span class="ex">The April finance memo predicts that the project will cost 7% more than the original estimate.</span><br /><span class="ex">According to the April finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more than the original estimate.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which active and passive pair share present progressive time?</li>
      <li>Which pair share present perfect aspect and a completed quantity?</li>
      <li>Which passive chain preserves a past obligation that was not met?</li>
      <li>Which reporting passive names the source and keeps the projected cost uncertain?</li>
      <li>What changes in the grammatical topic when active becomes passive?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You preserved progressive time, perfect result, a missed past obligation, sourced expectation, and the affected participant as passive topic.">
    <h3>Discovery check: recover the meaning carried by each chain</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Passive chain meaning choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is being replaced">is being replaced</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have been installed">have been installed</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should have been tested">should have been tested</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is expected to cost">is expected to cost</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="the affected participant becomes the grammatical topic">the affected participant becomes the grammatical topic</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The chain that presents replacement in progress now is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is being replaced" data-hint="Present progressive passive uses is plus being plus the participle." data-fix="The east elevator is being replaced." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The chain that presents 18 lights as completed output connected to now is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have been installed" data-hint="Present perfect passive uses have plus been plus the participle." data-fix="Eighteen lights have been installed." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The chain that preserves a missed past obligation is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should have been tested" data-hint="Should have marks the past obligation, and been tested makes its action passive." data-fix="The signs should have been tested." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>After the source phrase <span class="ex">According to the April finance memo</span>, the projected-cost reporting chain is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is expected to cost" data-hint="The project becomes the topic, and to cost belongs to the projected future relative to the current report." data-fix="The project is expected to cost 7% more than the original estimate." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Across every active-passive pair, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="the affected participant becomes the grammatical topic" data-hint="The event can remain the same while the clause begins with a different participant." data-fix="In a passive, the affected participant becomes the grammatical topic." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: preserve the auxiliary system</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Start from the active tense, aspect, or modal meaning. Keep that auxiliary system, insert the correct form of <span class="ex">be</span>, and place the lexical action in its past participle. The affected participant becomes the new subject and controls agreement.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>meaning</th><th>active</th><th>passive</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>present routine</td><td><span class="ex">They inspect the lifts.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lifts are inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>finished past</td><td><span class="ex">They inspected the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift was inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>present process</td><td><span class="ex">They are inspecting the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift is being inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>past process</td><td><span class="ex">They were inspecting the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift was being inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>present completed result</td><td><span class="ex">They have inspected the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift has been inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>earlier completed result</td><td><span class="ex">They had inspected the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift had been inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>future event</td><td><span class="ex">They will inspect the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift will be inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>future completed result</td><td><span class="ex">They will have inspected the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift will have been inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>present requirement</td><td><span class="ex">They must inspect the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift must be inspected.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>past criticism</td><td><span class="ex">They should have inspected the lift.</span></td><td><span class="ex">The lift should have been inspected.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The lexical participle does not carry tense by itself. In <span class="ex">will have been inspected</span>, <span class="ex">will</span> gives future reference, <span class="ex">have</span> gives perfect aspect, <span class="ex">been</span> realizes passive <span class="ex">be</span>, and <span class="ex">inspected</span> carries the action.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You preserved present and past progress, present and past perfect results, future completion, a modal requirement, and a past modal criticism.">
    <h3>Build the passive without losing time or aspect</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Passive tense and aspect choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is being inspected">is being inspected</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was being inspected">was being inspected</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has been inspected">has been inspected</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="had been inspected">had been inspected</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will have been inspected">will have been inspected</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must be inspected">must be inspected</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should have been inspected">should have been inspected</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will be inspected">will be inspected</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The inspection is in progress now: The east elevator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is being inspected" data-hint="Use present be plus being plus the participle for a passive process now." data-fix="The east elevator is being inspected now." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> now.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>At 10:00 yesterday, the inspection was in progress: The east elevator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was being inspected" data-hint="Put the progressive passive process at the finished past time with was being." data-fix="The east elevator was being inspected at 10:00 yesterday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at 10:00 yesterday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The inspection is complete and matters now: The east elevator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has been inspected" data-hint="Use has for present perfect and been plus participle for passive voice." data-fix="The east elevator has been inspected." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The inspection was complete before the director arrived: The elevator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="had been inspected" data-hint="Use had for the earlier past result, then been plus participle for passive voice." data-fix="The elevator had been inspected before the director arrived." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> before the director arrived.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The schedule predicts completion before the May 24 deadline: By May 24, every light <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will have been inspected" data-hint="Use future perfect passive for a result completed before a future deadline." data-fix="By May 24, every light will have been inspected." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The safety rule creates a present requirement: Every emergency sign <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must be inspected" data-hint="A modal passive uses must plus be plus the participle." data-fix="Every emergency sign must be inspected." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The review criticizes a missed inspection before opening day: Every sign <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should have been inspected" data-hint="Use should have for the missed past obligation and been inspected for passive voice." data-fix="Every sign should have been inspected before opening day." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> before opening day.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The schedule gives one future event, not a completed-before-deadline viewpoint: The west elevator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will be inspected" data-hint="Use will be plus participle for a straightforward future passive event." data-fix="The west elevator will be inspected next Tuesday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> next Tuesday.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the camera angle without hiding responsibility</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A passive is useful when the affected participant is already the topic, the agent is unknown, the agent is obvious from the procedure, or the result matters more than the actor. A named <span class="ex">by</span>-phrase is useful when identity, authority, method, discovery, or responsibility adds information.</p>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Agentless does not mean neutral</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">The deadline was missed</span> may be appropriate when the cause is genuinely unknown or the report is organized around the deadline. It can also conceal a known decision maker. If responsibility is relevant and supported, use active voice: <span class="ex">The project manager approved the late change, so the team missed the deadline.</span> Do not invent an agent, but do not delete a documented one merely to sound formal.</p>
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>reason for focus</th><th>defensible choice</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>unknown agent</td><td><span class="ex">A gate was damaged overnight.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>obvious routine agent</td><td><span class="ex">Tickets are checked at the entrance.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>qualified agent adds authority</td><td><span class="ex">The certificate was signed by engineer Lena Ortiz.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>known responsibility matters</td><td><span class="ex">The project director canceled the test.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>instrument, not agent</td><td><span class="ex">The panel was cut with a laser.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>source material, not agent</td><td><span class="ex">The bench was made from reclaimed wood.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You omitted unknown or routine agents, restored documented responsibility, retained a qualified agent, and separated by, with, and from.">
    <h3>Focus and responsibility decisions</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A gate was damaged overnight; the available record does not identify who damaged it." data-hint="Use an agentless passive because the affected gate is known but the actor is not." data-fix="A gate was damaged overnight; the available record does not identify who damaged it."><p class="quiz-question">1. Security footage shows the damage but not the person. Which sentence stays within the evidence?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A gate was damaged overnight; the available record does not identify who damaged it.">A gate was damaged overnight; the available record does not identify who damaged it.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A named maintenance worker damaged the gate, although no record identifies that worker.">A named maintenance worker damaged the gate, although no record identifies that worker.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The gate damaged someone overnight.">The gate damaged someone overnight.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Tickets are checked at the entrance." data-hint="The routine procedure and affected tickets matter; by staff adds no useful new information." data-fix="Tickets are checked at the entrance."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which concise sentence describes an ordinary entrance procedure without an unnecessary agent?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Tickets are checked at the entrance.">Tickets are checked at the entrance.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Tickets are checked by ticket-checking staff employees at the entrance.">Tickets are checked by ticket-checking staff employees at the entrance.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Tickets check the entrance by staff.">Tickets check the entrance by staff.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The project director canceled the documented safety test on April 9." data-hint="The signed decision record identifies a responsible decision maker, so active voice should keep that person visible." data-fix="The project director canceled the documented safety test on April 9."><p class="quiz-question">3. A signed record identifies who canceled a safety test, and that decision is central to the review. Which sentence uses focus responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The project director canceled the documented safety test on April 9.">The project director canceled the documented safety test on April 9.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The safety test was somehow canceled, and the documented decision maker is omitted.">The safety test was somehow canceled, and the documented decision maker is omitted.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="April 9 canceled the project director.">April 9 canceled the project director.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The safety certificate was signed by engineer Lena Ortiz." data-hint="The named engineer’s qualification makes the agent informative rather than redundant." data-fix="The safety certificate was signed by engineer Lena Ortiz."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which passive keeps the affected certificate as topic while adding the authoritative signer?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The safety certificate was signed by engineer Lena Ortiz.">The safety certificate was signed by engineer Lena Ortiz.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The safety certificate was signed with engineer Lena Ortiz.">The safety certificate was signed with engineer Lena Ortiz.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Engineer Lena Ortiz was signed from the certificate.">Engineer Lena Ortiz was signed from the certificate.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The metal panel was cut with a laser." data-hint="A laser is the instrument used to perform the action, not the acting agent." data-fix="The metal panel was cut with a laser."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence labels the instrument accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The metal panel was cut with a laser.">The metal panel was cut with a laser.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The metal panel was cut by a laser as a responsible person.">The metal panel was cut by a laser as a responsible person.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The laser was made from the metal panel.">The laser was made from the metal panel.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The waiting-room bench was made from reclaimed wood." data-hint="The original material was transformed into the finished bench, so use from." data-fix="The waiting-room bench was made from reclaimed wood."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which sentence identifies transformed source material rather than an agent?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The waiting-room bench was made from reclaimed wood.">The waiting-room bench was made from reclaimed wood.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The waiting-room bench was made by reclaimed wood as the decision maker.">The waiting-room bench was made by reclaimed wood as the decision maker.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Reclaimed wood was made with the waiting room.">Reclaimed wood was made with the waiting room.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep grammatical chains readable</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The passive system can theoretically combine several layers. Some combinations are grammatical but hard to process. <span class="ex">The permit has been being reviewed for six weeks</span> is possible, but many speakers prefer <span class="ex">The permit review has been underway for six weeks</span> or, when the reviewer matters, <span class="ex">The committee has been reviewing the permit for six weeks</span>.</p>
  <p>Likewise, <span class="ex">The bridge may be being inspected now</span> is grammatical, but <span class="ex">Inspectors may be checking the bridge now</span> is often clearer. Recasting is an information-design choice, not proof that the longer chain is ungrammatical.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retained natural progressive, future-perfect, and modal-perfect passives while recasting two grammatical but overloaded chains for clarity.">
    <h3>Use the full system, then edit for processing load</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Passive-chain editing choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is being reviewed">is being reviewed</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will have been installed">will have been installed</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should have been sent">should have been sent</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The permit review has been underway for six weeks">The permit review has been underway for six weeks</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Inspectors may be checking the bridge now">Inspectors may be checking the bridge now</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The ordinary present progressive passive is concise enough: The application <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is being reviewed" data-hint="This three-part chain is a normal way to show a passive process now." data-fix="The application is being reviewed." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The future deadline genuinely requires future perfect passive: By Friday, every sign <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="will have been installed" data-hint="The sentence needs a passive result completed before a future deadline." data-fix="By Friday, every sign will have been installed." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The review criticizes a missing earlier email: The notice <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should have been sent" data-hint="Keep should have for past criticism and been sent for passive voice." data-fix="The notice should have been sent on Monday." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on Monday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Choose the clear recast when the six-week activity matters more than the reviewer: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The permit review has been underway for six weeks" data-hint="Replace has been being reviewed with a clear noun plus has been underway." data-fix="The permit review has been underway for six weeks." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Choose the clear active recast when the possible current agent can be named generically: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Inspectors may be checking the bridge now" data-hint="Keep the possibility and current process while moving the known generic agent into subject position." data-fix="Inspectors may be checking the bridge now." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Event, result state, and conversational <span class="ex">get</span></h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A form of <span class="ex">be + participle</span> can describe an event or a resulting state. <span class="ex">The guard closed the gate at 9:00</span> clearly describes an event. <span class="ex">At 9:15, the gate was closed</span> can describe its state at that time. Wider context, a named agent, an event-time expression, or an adverb can guide the reading.</p>
  <p>A <span class="ex">get</span>-passive often sounds more conversational and dynamic: <span class="ex">The package got damaged during transit</span>. It frequently foregrounds what happened to the affected participant, sometimes with an adverse or unexpected effect. Neutral formal reporting usually prefers <span class="ex">was damaged</span>. Do not use <span class="ex">get</span> to replace every passive.</p>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished a documented event, a resulting condition, a conversational affected-participant event, a neutral formal passive, and an ordinary adjective-like schedule state.">
    <h3>Interpret the passive from the whole context</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The gate was closed by the guard at exactly 9:00." data-hint="The named agent and exact event time make the closing event central." data-fix="The gate was closed by the guard at exactly 9:00."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence clearly presents a closing event?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The gate was closed by the guard at exactly 9:00.">The gate was closed by the guard at exactly 9:00.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="At 9:15, the gate was in a closed condition.">At 9:15, the gate was in a closed condition.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The gate is usually closed on Sundays.">The gate is usually closed on Sundays.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="When we arrived at 9:15, the gate was closed, so we could not enter." data-hint="The arrival context describes the condition encountered at 9:15, not necessarily the closing event." data-fix="When we arrived, the gate was closed, so we could not enter."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence foregrounds the resulting state at arrival?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When we arrived at 9:15, the gate was closed, so we could not enter.">When we arrived at 9:15, the gate was closed, so we could not enter.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The guard actively closed the gate at exactly 9:00.">The guard actively closed the gate at exactly 9:00.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The gate had been closing the guard.">The gate had been closing the guard.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="My package got damaged during the move." data-hint="Use get for a conversational account of an unwanted event affecting the package." data-fix="My package got damaged during the move."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence naturally foregrounds an unfortunate event in conversation?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="My package got damaged during the move.">My package got damaged during the move.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="My package got damage during the move.">My package got damage during the move.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="My package was getting the movers damaged.">My package was getting the movers damaged.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The package was damaged during transit, according to the carrier’s inspection record." data-hint="A neutral formal record normally uses be plus the participle rather than conversational get." data-fix="The package was damaged during transit, according to the carrier’s inspection record."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence suits a neutral written claim with a named source?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The package was damaged during transit, according to the carrier’s inspection record.">The package was damaged during transit, according to the carrier’s inspection record.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The package kinda got messed up somehow, definitely.">The package kinda got messed up somehow, definitely.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Transit damaged and got the package by the record.">Transit damaged and got the package by the record.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The office is closed on Sundays." data-hint="The sentence gives a regular schedule state without presenting one particular closing action." data-fix="The office is closed on Sundays."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which sentence describes an ordinary schedule condition rather than one specific closing event?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The office is closed on Sundays.">The office is closed on Sundays.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The manager closed the office at 6:03 last Sunday.">The manager closed the office at 6:03 last Sunday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The office has been closing the manager every Sunday.">The office has been closing the manager every Sunday.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use two-object and prepositional passives naturally</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>With verbs such as <span class="ex">give, send, offer, show, tell</span>, either object may sometimes become the passive subject. Choose the version that matches the continuing topic.</p>
  <p><span class="ex">The project office gave residents written notice.</span><br /><span class="ex">Residents were given written notice.</span><br /><span class="ex">Written notice was given to residents.</span></p>
  <p>A passive can also promote the object of a required preposition. Keep that preposition: <span class="ex">The team dealt with the complaint → The complaint was dealt with</span>; <span class="ex">People have talked about the delay → The delay has been talked about</span>. Grammatical does not always mean elegant, so recast when a promoted phrase sounds forced or hides the clearer agent.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You selected resident-topic and notice-topic passives, retained required prepositions, and recast one technically possible but unhelpful passive.">
    <h3>Keep the intended topic and required preposition</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Two-object and prepositional passive choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Residents were given written notice">Residents were given written notice</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Written notice was given to residents">Written notice was given to residents</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="was dealt with">was dealt with</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has been talked about">has been talked about</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Several residents objected to the proposal">Several residents objected to the proposal</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The paragraph continues to describe residents and what they received: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Residents were given written notice" data-hint="Make residents the passive subject because they remain the paragraph topic." data-fix="Residents were given written notice." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The paragraph continues to describe the notice and its distribution: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Written notice was given to residents" data-hint="Make written notice the subject and retain to before the receiving group." data-fix="Written notice was given to residents." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Retain the required preposition in the passive: The complaint <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="was dealt with" data-hint="Deal requires with; the preposition remains after the participle." data-fix="The complaint was dealt with promptly." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> promptly.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Keep <span class="ex">about</span> after the passive chain: The delay <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has been talked about" data-hint="Talk about remains a unit when the delay becomes passive subject." data-fix="The delay has been talked about for weeks." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> for weeks.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Choose the clearer active sentence when the objectors are known and responsible for the objection: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Several residents objected to the proposal" data-hint="The possible passive The proposal was objected to is formal and hides the more useful known objectors here." data-fix="Several residents objected to the proposal." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Report claims without changing their time or certainty</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Reporting passives let a writer foreground either a whole proposition or the reported person or thing. They do not make a claim true. Name a source when readers need to judge it, and preserve words such as <span class="ex">reportedly, allegedly, according to</span>, or a specific reporting verb when certainty is limited.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>information focus</th><th>pattern</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>whole proposition</td><td><span class="ex">It + passive reporting verb + that-clause</span></td><td><span class="ex">It is reported that the station is on schedule.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>person or thing as topic</td><td><span class="ex">subject + passive reporting verb + infinitive</span></td><td><span class="ex">The station is reported to be on schedule.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>simultaneous state or routine</td><td><span class="ex">to be / to + base verb</span></td><td><span class="ex">The station is believed to be safe. The system is said to work well.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>ongoing event at reporting time</td><td><span class="ex">to be + -ing</span></td><td><span class="ex">Costs are thought to be rising.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>earlier completed active event</td><td><span class="ex">to have + participle</span></td><td><span class="ex">The firm is alleged to have withheld a report.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>earlier ongoing event</td><td><span class="ex">to have been + -ing</span></td><td><span class="ex">The firm is reported to have been negotiating for months.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>earlier passive event</td><td><span class="ex">to have been + participle</span></td><td><span class="ex">The gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="note">
    <h3>Do not mix the two reporting frames</h3>
    <p>Use <span class="ex">It is believed that the project is late</span> or <span class="ex">The project is believed to be late</span>. Do not combine them as <span class="ex">The project is believed that it is late</span>. The report time also matters: <span class="ex">At the time, it was believed that the plan was safe</span> reports a past belief and does not claim that people still hold it now.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You kept impersonal and personal frames separate and matched simultaneous, ongoing, earlier completed, earlier ongoing, earlier passive, and past-belief time relationships.">
    <h3>Choose the reporting frame and infinitive time</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Passive reporting choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It is reported that the station is on schedule">It is reported that the station is on schedule</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The station is reported to be on schedule">The station is reported to be on schedule</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is thought to be rising">is thought to be rising</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is alleged to have withheld">is alleged to have withheld</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is reported to have been negotiating">is reported to have been negotiating</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is believed to have been damaged">is believed to have been damaged</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="At the time, it was believed that the plan was safe">At the time, it was believed that the plan was safe</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="According to the April finance memo">According to the April finance memo</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Foreground the whole proposition: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It is reported that the station is on schedule" data-hint="Use impersonal it, a passive reporting verb, and a complete that-clause." data-fix="It is reported that the station is on schedule." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Keep the station as the paragraph topic: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The station is reported to be on schedule" data-hint="Make the station the subject and follow the passive reporting verb with to be." data-fix="The station is reported to be on schedule." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The finance memo describes a cost increase in progress at reporting time: The final cost <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is thought to be rising" data-hint="Use to be plus -ing for an activity ongoing relative to the current report." data-fix="The final cost is thought to be rising." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The allegation concerns a completed earlier active action: The firm <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is alleged to have withheld" data-hint="Use to have plus the participle withheld for an alleged action earlier than the current report." data-fix="The firm is alleged to have withheld a report." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> a report.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The report concerns an earlier activity continuing across several months: The firm <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is reported to have been negotiating" data-hint="Use to have been plus -ing for an earlier ongoing activity." data-fix="The firm is reported to have been negotiating for months." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> for months.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The claim concerns an earlier event in which the gate received damage: The gate <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is believed to have been damaged" data-hint="Use to have been plus the participle damaged for an earlier passive event." data-fix="The gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> during delivery.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>Report only a historical belief, without implying that it is still accepted: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="At the time, it was believed that the plan was safe" data-hint="Use past was believed and the explicit time frame At the time." data-fix="At the time, it was believed that the plan was safe." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>Name the source before a forecast that readers must evaluate: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="According to the April finance memo" data-hint="Choose the phrase that identifies the specific document supporting the expectation." data-fix="According to the April finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, the project is expected to cost 7% more.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Sound natural: keep the small words recoverable</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In ordinary U.S. speech, auxiliaries often weaken while the lexical participle carries strong information stress: <span class="ex">has been apPROVED</span> /həz bɪn əˈpruvd/; <span class="ex">should have been SENT</span> /ʃʊd əv bɪn sɛnt/. In <span class="ex">is being reVIEWED</span>, keep <span class="ex">being</span> distinct from <span class="ex">been</span> because it preserves progressive aspect.</p>
  <p>Compare <span class="ex">They’ve been reviewing the files</span>, an active ongoing process, with <span class="ex">They’ve been reviewed</span>, a passive completed result about <span class="ex">they</span>. The form after <span class="ex">been</span> and the surrounding noun meaning help the listener recover the structure. In a <span class="ex">by</span>-phrase, unstressed <span class="ex">by</span> may weaken toward /bə/, but stress the agent when identity is the new contrast.</p>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read weak auxiliaries, been-being contrast, active-passive contrast, reduced by, and reporting thought-group listening check" data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the perfect passive, modal-perfect passive, progressive marker being, active continuous, and contrastively important agent.">
    <h3>Listen before opening the transcript</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Ask your tutor to read the five lines naturally. Choose the complete meaning or form, then open the transcript only after checking.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Spoken passive choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has been approved">has been approved</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should have been sent">should have been sent</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is being reviewed">is being reviewed</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have been reviewing">have been reviewing</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="engineer Lena Ortiz">engineer Lena Ortiz</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 1:</span> <span class="ex">The permit has been approved.</span> Recover the complete perfect passive: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has been approved" data-hint="Listen through weak has and been to the stressed participle approved." data-fix="The complete chain is has been approved." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 2:</span> <span class="ex">The notice should have been sent Monday.</span> Recover the missed past obligation: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should have been sent" data-hint="Keep should, weak have, been, and the stressed participle sent." data-fix="The complete modal-perfect passive is should have been sent." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 3:</span> <span class="ex">The application is being reviewed.</span> The word that preserves progressive aspect belongs in <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="is being reviewed" data-hint="Listen for being, not been, between is and reviewed." data-fix="Is being reviewed is the present progressive passive." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 4:</span> <span class="ex">They’ve been reviewing the files.</span> The subject performs an ongoing active process, so the chain is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have been reviewing" data-hint="The -ing form reviewing after been creates active present perfect continuous." data-fix="They have been reviewing the files." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="contraction">Tutor line 5:</span> <span class="ex">The certificate was signed by ENGINEER LENA ORTIZ, not the contractor.</span> The contrastively important new agent is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="engineer Lena Ortiz" data-hint="The strong contrast corrects the signer’s identity." data-fix="Engineer Lena Ortiz is the contrastively stressed agent." data-placeholder="listen">listen</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    <details>
      <summary>Tutor script and transcript</summary>
      <ol>
        <li>The permit has been approved.</li>
        <li>The notice should have been sent Monday.</li>
        <li>The application is being reviewed.</li>
        <li>They’ve been reviewing the files.</li>
        <li>The certificate was signed by <strong>engineer Lena Ortiz</strong>, not the contractor.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Read each line once at a natural pace. Repeat once if requested. Then contrast <span class="ex">has been approved</span>, <span class="ex">is being reviewed</span>, and <span class="ex">has been reviewing</span> while the learner identifies the meaning of every small auxiliary.</p>
    </details>
  </div>

  <h2>Read a project record with source and responsibility intact</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Northbank station accessibility file</h3>
    <p>The access upgrade began on January 8. At the April 16 review, the east elevator was being replaced. Eighteen of 24 platform lights had been installed, and the remaining six lights had been delivered on April 15 but had not been tested. The review required all six to be tested before the platform could reopen.</p>
    <p>A delivery log records that one passenger gate was damaged on April 2, but the log does not identify the person who caused the damage. A signed decision sheet shows that project director Rafael Kim canceled an April 9 emergency-sign test so the same crew could complete another task. Because the responsible decision maker is documented and relevant, the review states this action in active voice.</p>
    <p>The April 15 finance memo predicts a final cost 7% above the original estimate. According to that memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more, but the final total is not yet known. The contractor’s review says late parts are believed to have contributed to the schedule change. Supplier logs support a contribution, not the claim that late parts were the only cause.</p>
    <p>The revised schedule says the six lights will have been tested by May 24 and the station will reopen on June 1. These are scheduled outcomes, not completed facts. The April 16 review was published on April 18 and signed by engineer Lena Ortiz.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You recovered the current passive process, completed quantity, untested requirement, documented active responsibility, sourced cost forecast, and limited causal claim.">
    <h3>Evidence check: form, focus, and certainty</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The east elevator was being replaced at the April 16 review." data-hint="Recover the passive process that was in progress at the past review time." data-fix="The east elevator was being replaced at the April 16 review."><p class="quiz-question">1. What passive process was in progress at the April 16 review?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The east elevator was being replaced at the April 16 review.">The east elevator was being replaced at the April 16 review.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The east elevator had reopened before work began in January.">The east elevator had reopened before work began in January.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The east elevator was replacing the project director.">The east elevator was replacing the project director.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Eighteen of 24 platform lights had been installed, while six delivered lights had not been tested." data-hint="Recover both the completed installed quantity and the negative perfect-passive test status." data-fix="Eighteen lights had been installed; the remaining six had been delivered but not tested."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which status statement is accurate at the review time?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Eighteen of 24 platform lights had been installed, while six delivered lights had not been tested.">Eighteen of 24 platform lights had been installed, while six delivered lights had not been tested.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All 24 lights had been tested and opened before January 8.">All 24 lights had been tested and opened before January 8.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Six lights had tested the other 18 platform lights.">Six lights had tested the other 18 platform lights.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Project director Rafael Kim canceled the April 9 test, according to the signed decision sheet." data-hint="The review has a named responsible decision maker and a signed source, so active voice keeps responsibility visible." data-fix="Project director Rafael Kim canceled the April 9 test, according to the signed decision sheet."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence reports the documented cancellation responsibly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Project director Rafael Kim canceled the April 9 test, according to the signed decision sheet.">Project director Rafael Kim canceled the April 9 test, according to the signed decision sheet.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The test was somehow canceled, although the signed decision maker is central and known.">The test was somehow canceled, although the signed decision maker is central and known.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Engineer Lena Ortiz canceled every test, although the decision sheet names someone else.">Engineer Lena Ortiz canceled every test, although the decision sheet names someone else.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="According to the April 15 finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more, but the final total is not yet known." data-hint="Keep the named source, forecast status, exact percentage, and unknown final total." data-fix="The finance memo forecasts a 7% increase; the final total is not yet known."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which cost statement preserves source and uncertainty?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="According to the April 15 finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more, but the final total is not yet known.">According to the April 15 finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more, but the final total is not yet known.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The project definitely cost exactly 7% more before it began, and no source is needed.">The project definitely cost exactly 7% more before it began, and no source is needed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Seven projects are believed to have cost one station.">Seven projects are believed to have cost one station.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Late parts are believed to have contributed to the schedule change, but the records do not establish them as the only cause." data-hint="Preserve the perfect infinitive for an earlier contribution and the explicit limit on sole causation." data-fix="The records support a contribution from late parts, not the claim that they were the only cause."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which causal statement stays within the contractor review and supplier logs?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Late parts are believed to have contributed to the schedule change, but the records do not establish them as the only cause.">Late parts are believed to have contributed to the schedule change, but the records do not establish them as the only cause.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Late parts certainly caused every delay and prove that no decision contributed.">Late parts certainly caused every delay and prove that no decision contributed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because the cause is limited, supplier records contain no useful evidence.">Because the cause is limited, supplier records contain no useful evidence.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The lights will have been tested by May 24 is a scheduled future result, not a completed fact on April 16." data-hint="Future perfect passive projects completion before a future deadline; it does not report present completion." data-fix="The schedule projects that testing will be complete by May 24."><p class="quiz-question">6. How should the May 24 passive be interpreted at the April 16 review?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The lights will have been tested by May 24 is a scheduled future result, not a completed fact on April 16.">The lights will have been tested by May 24 is a scheduled future result, not a completed fact on April 16.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The lights had already been tested on April 16 because future perfect always describes present fact.">The lights had already been tested on April 16 because future perfect always describes present fact.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The lights will test the calendar by May 24.">The lights will test the calendar by May 24.</button></div></div>
    </div>
