  </div>

  <h2>Build form, focus, and reporting time</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the remaining lights should have been tested before the review" data-hint="Begin with the affected lights, keep should have for past criticism, and add been plus the participle tested." data-fix="The remaining lights should have been tested before the review." data-success-message="Correct. Should have preserves the missed past obligation, while been tested keeps the required action passive.">
    <h3>Builder 1: modal-perfect passive</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the review’s criticism.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="been">been</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the review">the review</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="The remaining lights">The remaining lights</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="tested">tested</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="should">should</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="before">before</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap chunks in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the signed decision sheet shows that rafael kim canceled the test" data-hint="Keep the documentary source first and use active voice to retain the responsible decision maker." data-fix="The signed decision sheet shows that Rafael Kim canceled the test." data-success-message="Correct. The active that-clause keeps the documented decision maker visible instead of hiding responsibility in an agentless passive.">
    <h3>Builder 2: source plus responsible active voice</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the evidence-based responsibility statement.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="the test">the test</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="shows">shows</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="Rafael Kim">Rafael Kim</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="The signed decision sheet">The signed decision sheet</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="canceled">canceled</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="that">that</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap chunks in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery" data-hint="Make the gate the reporting topic, use to have been for an earlier passive event, and finish with the event context." data-fix="The gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery." data-success-message="Correct. Is believed creates the current report, while to have been damaged places the passive damage event earlier.">
    <h3>Builder 3: earlier passive event inside a report</h3><p class="tile-target">Build the personal reporting passive.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank><button class="tile" data-build-tile="during delivery">during delivery</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="to have been">to have been</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="The gate">The gate</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="damaged">damaged</button><button class="tile" data-build-tile="is believed">is believed</button></div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap chunks in order"></div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair the broken layer</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="reviewed" data-hint="An action in progress now requires being between is and reviewed." data-fix="The application is being reviewed now." data-why="Present progressive passive uses present be plus being plus the past participle." data-success-message="Correct. Is being reviewed now preserves both progressive aspect and passive voice.">
    <h3>Repair 1: restore progressive aspect</h3><p>Tap the word where the missing layer becomes visible.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="application">The application</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="reviewed">reviewed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="now">now.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="selected" data-hint="Present perfect passive needs have been before the participle selected." data-fix="Three candidates have been selected for interview." data-why="Have carries present perfect aspect; been realizes passive be; selected is the lexical participle." data-success-message="Correct. Have been selected now preserves perfect aspect and passive voice.">
    <h3>Repair 2: restore passive <span class="ex">been</span></h3><p>Tap the word whose chain is incomplete.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="candidates">Three candidates</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have">have</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="selected">selected</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="interview">for interview.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="that" data-hint="A personal reporting passive takes an infinitive, not a that-clause after the reported subject." data-fix="The director is reported to have resigned. Alternatively: It is reported that the director resigned." data-why="Keep the personal subject plus infinitive frame separate from impersonal it plus a that-clause." data-success-message="Correct. The repair separates the personal and impersonal reporting frames and preserves the earlier resignation time.">
    <h3>Repair 3: separate reporting frames</h3><p>Tap the connector that wrongly combines two structures.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="director">The director</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="reported">is reported</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="that">that</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="resigned">she resigned.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="was canceled" data-hint="The signed sheet identifies Rafael Kim, and responsibility is central, so restore the documented agent in active voice." data-fix="According to the signed decision sheet, Rafael Kim canceled the test." data-why="An agentless passive is grammatically possible, but it is an irresponsible information choice when a relevant responsible decision maker is documented." data-success-message="Correct. The active revision now keeps the signed source and responsible decision maker visible.">
    <h3>Repair 4: restore documented responsibility</h3><p>Tap the phrase whose agentless focus is misleading in this context.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="source">According to the signed decision sheet,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="test">the test</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="was canceled">was canceled</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="date">on April 9.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Practice institutional language without exposing private information</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to discuss a real disciplinary investigation, accusation, medical record, financial dispute, immigration process, legal matter, confidential workplace event, or identifiable person. Use Northbank, a public document with reliable sourcing, or a tutor-created fictional case. The goal is information focus and evidence control, not formal-sounding secrecy.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Auxiliary audit:</b> Mark future, perfect, progressive, modal, passive <span class="ex">be</span>, and lexical participle in one long chain. Remove any layer only if the meaning changes appropriately.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Camera choice:</b> Retell one event with the affected participant as topic, then with the documented agent as topic. Explain which version better serves the paragraph.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Responsibility challenge:</b> Your partner asks, <span class="ex">Do we know who did this, and does that identity matter?</span> Restore the agent, keep it unknown, or state the evidence limit.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Reporting-time ladder:</b> Use one current state, one ongoing event, one earlier completed action, and one earlier passive event after a personal reporting passive.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register edit:</b> Recast one heavy grammatical chain for a public briefing without losing its time, aspect, modality, or certainty.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: deliver a 90-second sourced project briefing</h3>
    <p>Use Northbank or another tutor-supplied fictional file. Include a passive process in progress, a completed passive result, a negative perfect passive, a future or future-perfect passive, and a modal-perfect passive. Keep one known responsible agent in active voice and one qualified agent in a useful <span class="ex">by</span>-phrase. Add one result-state or conversational <span class="ex">get</span>-passive only if the register supports it. Use one two-object or prepositional passive. Report one simultaneous claim and one earlier claim with different infinitive forms. Name the source, calibrate certainty, and recast one overloaded chain. When the editor challenges an agentless clause, justify it or restore the agent.</p>
    <p><b>Success criteria:</b> Can the listener recover the topic, agent status, tense, aspect, modality, event or state reading, reporting time, source, certainty, documented responsibility, and projected versus completed status without a missing auxiliary, mixed reporting frame, or false implication of proof?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved tense and aspect, responsible focus, readable chain design, passive event time inside reporting, sourced uncertainty, and active-passive listening contrast.">
    <h3>Final check: preserve grammar and information ethics</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="By May 24, all six lights will have been tested." data-hint="Use future perfect passive for a projected result completed before the future deadline." data-fix="By May 24, all six lights will have been tested."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence has the complete future-perfect passive chain?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="By May 24, all six lights will have been tested.">By May 24, all six lights will have been tested.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="By May 24, all six lights will been have test.">By May 24, all six lights will been have test.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="By May 24, all six lights have testing future.">By May 24, all six lights have testing future.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="According to the signed sheet, Rafael Kim canceled the test on April 9." data-hint="Use active voice because the documented responsible decision maker is relevant to the review." data-fix="According to the signed sheet, Rafael Kim canceled the test on April 9."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence keeps documented responsibility visible?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="According to the signed sheet, Rafael Kim canceled the test on April 9.">According to the signed sheet, Rafael Kim canceled the test on April 9.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The test was canceled by nobody worth naming, although the signed sheet identifies the central decision maker.">The test was canceled by nobody worth naming, although the signed sheet identifies the central decision maker.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="April 9 was canceled by the test.">April 9 was canceled by the test.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The permit review has been underway for six weeks." data-hint="Recast the grammatical but overloaded has been being reviewed chain without losing its six-week continuing duration." data-fix="The permit review has been underway for six weeks."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which concise sentence preserves the meaning of <span class="ex">The permit has been being reviewed for six weeks</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The permit review has been underway for six weeks.">The permit review has been underway for six weeks.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The permit was reviewed for six weeks, so the current process is definitely finished.">The permit was reviewed for six weeks, so the current process is definitely finished.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Six weeks have reviewed the permit.">Six weeks have reviewed the permit.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery." data-hint="Use to have been plus participle for an earlier event in which the gate received the action." data-fix="The gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which personal reporting passive places a passive damage event before the current belief?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery.">The gate is believed to have been damaged during delivery.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The gate is believed that it damaged delivery.">The gate is believed that it damaged delivery.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It believes the gate to damaged during delivery.">It believes the gate to damaged during delivery.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="According to the finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more, but the final total is not yet known." data-hint="Retain the named source, expectation rather than fact, exact forecast, and unknown final outcome." data-fix="The finance memo forecasts a 7% increase; the final total remains unknown."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which reporting sentence calibrates certainty accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="According to the finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more, but the final total is not yet known.">According to the finance memo, the project is expected to cost 7% more, but the final total is not yet known.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The project is proven to cost exactly 7% more forever because expectations are facts.">The project is proven to cost exactly 7% more forever because expectations are facts.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="No source should be named because passive reporting automatically proves the claim.">No source should be named because passive reporting automatically proves the claim.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="They’ve been reviewing is active and ongoing; they’ve been reviewed is passive and presents a completed result about them." data-hint="Use the -ing form after been for the active ongoing process and the participle after been for the passive result." data-fix="They have been reviewing is active continuous; they have been reviewed is passive perfect."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which explanation distinguishes the two reduced U.S. speech chains?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They’ve been reviewing is active and ongoing; they’ve been reviewed is passive and presents a completed result about them.">They’ve been reviewing is active and ongoing; they’ve been reviewed is passive and presents a completed result about them.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both chains are identical because reviewing and reviewed have the same form and role.">Both chains are identical because reviewing and reviewed have the same form and role.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They’ve always means they would, regardless of the following verb.">They’ve always means they would, regardless of the following verb.</button></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect: can you defend the camera angle?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the passive decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">The clause topic is...</span> <span class="ex">The agent is known / unknown / obvious / relevant because...</span> <span class="ex">The auxiliary that carries time is...</span> <span class="ex">The aspect is...</span> <span class="ex">The passive be is...</span> <span class="ex">The lexical participle is...</span> <span class="ex">This is an event / result state / get-passive because...</span> <span class="ex">The reporting time is...</span> <span class="ex">The source supports...</span> <span class="ex">The source does not prove...</span></p>
    <p>Then take one sentence from your fictional briefing. Draw boxes around every auxiliary and underline the participle. Retell it actively. If the focus changes in a harmful way, explain why the passive is justified; if responsibility becomes clearer, keep the active revision.</p>
    <p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p>
  </div>

